= High-Yield Chronology & Personalities

- *27 May 1964:* Jawaharlal Nehru passes away; Lal Bahadur Shastri takes oath as Prime Minister.
- *September 1965:* Indo-Pak War; Shastri coins *"Jai Jawan, Jai Kisan"*.
- *10 January 1966:* Tashkent Agreement signed; Shastri dies suddenly in Tashkent.
- *January 1966:* Indira Gandhi defeats Morarji Desai in secret ballot (355–169) to become PM.
- *June 1966:* Devaluation of Indian Rupee under World Bank pressure.
- *February 1967:* Fourth General Elections ("Political Earthquake"); Congress loses 8 states; SVD coalitions arise.
- *May 1967:* Indira Gandhi floats the Ten-Point Programme.
- *May 1969:* President Zakir Husain passes away.
- *July 1969:* Indira nationalises 14 major commercial banks; Morarji Desai resigns.
- *August 1969:* V.V. Giri elected President of India via "conscience vote", defeating official nominee N. Sanjeeva Reddy.
- *November 1969:* Congress formally splits into Congress (O) and Congress (R).
- *December 1970:* Fifth Lok Sabha dissolved ahead of term.
- *March 1971:* Fifth General Elections; Congress (R) sweeps 352 seats on the slogan *"Garibi Hatao"*.
- *December 1971:* Indo-Pak War leads to the liberation of Bangladesh; Congress dominance consecrated.

