= Practice Questions (Exam Pattern)

Ten questions in the authentic CUET UG single-correct style. The official marking scheme awards $+5$ for each correct answer and deducts $-1$ for every incorrect answer.

#mcq(1, [Who succeeded Jawaharlal Nehru as the Prime Minister of India in May 1964?], (
  [Morarji Desai], [Gulzarilal Nanda], [Lal Bahadur Shastri], [K. Kamaraj],
))

#mcq(2, [The famous slogan "Jai Jawan, Jai Kisan" was coined by Lal Bahadur Shastri during the:], (
  [1962 Sino-Indian War], [1965 Indo-Pak War], [1967 General Elections], [First Five Year Plan launch],
))

#mcq(3, [The term "Non-Congressism" was propounded in 1967 by which political thinker and leader?], (
  [Jayaprakash Narayan], [C. Rajagopalachari], [Dr. Rammanohar Lohia], [Acharya Kripalani],
))

#mcq(4, [In the 1967 Fourth General Elections, Congress failed to secure an absolute majority in how many state legislative assemblies?], (
  [Four states], [Six states], [Seven states], [Ten states],
))

#mcq(5, [The infamous phrase "Aaya Ram, Gaya Ram" entered Indian political vocabulary following repeated defections by an MLA named Gaya Lal in which state?], (
  [Punjab], [Uttar Pradesh], [Haryana], [Bihar],
))

#mcq(6, [How many major commercial banks were nationalised by an executive ordinance promulgated by Indira Gandhi in July 1969?], (
  [10 banks], [14 banks], [20 banks], [8 banks],
))

#mcq(7, [In the historic 1969 Presidential Election, who won the presidency as an Independent candidate backed by Indira Gandhi's call for a "conscience vote"?], (
  [N. Sanjeeva Reddy], [V.V. Giri], [Fakhruddin Ali Ahmed], [Dr. Zakir Husain],
))

#mcq(8, [Following the split of the Indian National Congress in November 1969, the faction led by the Syndicate was known as:], (
  [Congress (R)], [Congress (O)], [Congress (I)], [Congress (S)],
))

#mcq(9, [What was the central election slogan deployed by Indira Gandhi to counter the Grand Alliance's "Indira Hatao" in the 1971 General Elections?], (
  [Jai Jawan Jai Kisan], [Garibi Hatao], [Sampoorn Kranti], [Congress Lao, Desh Bachao],
))

#mcq(10, [In the 1971 Fifth Lok Sabha elections, how many seats did Indira Gandhi's Congress (R) win on its own?], (
  [283 seats], [352 seats], [375 seats], [414 seats],
))

= Detailed Solutions

#solution(1, [Lal Bahadur Shastri succeeded Nehru as Prime Minister in June 1964 following a unanimous consensus process led by Congress President K. Kamaraj. Gulzarilal Nanda served only as interim PM for a few days.], answer: [C])

#solution(2, [Shastri coined "Jai Jawan, Jai Kisan" during the 1965 war with Pakistan to salute the dual pillars of national defense and food self-sufficiency during the agrarian crisis.], answer: [B])

#solution(3, [Dr. Rammanohar Lohia, the veteran socialist theoretician, propounded "Non-Congressism" to unite the fragmented opposition vote and overthrow the Congress monopoly.], answer: [C])

#solution(4, [Congress failed to get a majority in 7 states directly in the elections, and lost an 8th (Haryana) to immediate defections, creating a non-Congress belt in 8 state assemblies.], answer: [C])

#solution(5, [Gaya Lal was an MLA from Hassanpur in Haryana who switched parties three times within a fortnight in 1967, giving birth to Rao Birender Singh's famous quip "Gaya Ram is now Aaya Ram".], answer: [C])

#solution(6, [Indira Gandhi nationalised 14 major private commercial banks in July 1969 through an emergency ordinance, triggering the resignation of Deputy PM and Finance Minister Morarji Desai.], answer: [B])

#solution(7, [V.V. Giri won the 1969 election as an Independent candidate against the official Congress nominee N. Sanjeeva Reddy after Indira called for a "conscience vote".], answer: [B])

#solution(8, [The Syndicate faction was designated Congress (Organisation) or Congress (O), while Indira Gandhi's breakaway party was designated Congress (Requisitionists) or Congress (R).], answer: [B])

#solution(9, [Indira Gandhi countered the opposition's negative "Indira Hatao" with her famous populist pledge "Garibi Hatao" (Abolish Poverty), clinching a nationwide pro-poor vote base.], answer: [B])

#solution(10, [Congress (R) won 352 seats on its own (and 375 together with ally CPI), completely decimating the Grand Alliance and proving that Indira's party was the real Congress.], answer: [B])

